{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"4e71414da934c23a","type":"text","text":"```text\n New design flow:\n *Primary key generation*\n\t1. In table metadata(every table) i have this object called \"data\" in that object I have another object called \"possible_pk\". Instead of taking all the columns in table metadata.\n\t2. I will then pass the all the contexts what am passing currently as in business context, topic-labeled context, table context, columns (which are present in possible_pk)\n\t3. I ask LLM to select pick the matched primary key for this table.. There may be 2 or more primary keys for single table.\n\t4. I store that primary key in its table.\n\t5. I iterate same for all the tables present.\n```\n\n\n```\nNew design flow\n*Foreign key generation*\n1. After processing primary keys for all the tables, i start generating foreign keys..\n2. For foreign keys, first i get the primary key for particular table, you need to make the search whether this primary key is present in other table's column. For search i have two types of search.\n\t1. Exact match: For exact match i do the key word match. I will check whether this primary key is present in the columns field.\n\t2. Semantic match: Same logic how i am doing it currently. Get top 2 results by searching using search query and then i will pass that to LLM check which is the best possible candidate for foreign key, if not any return null. \n\t3. Next I need to write the other two objects which are primary_keys_referencing_tables and foreign_key_referencing_tables.. \n\t\t   1. I will now explain schema, and logic for PKRT and FKRT.\n\t\t      * After finding the foreign key of a table i then write the primary key referencing table in the source table and foreign key referencing table in target table.\n\t\t\tFor example: \n\t\t\tI have two tables COA and GL where COA have c1(primary key), c2, c3 columns and GL have c9(primary key),c8,c3 columns. Below is the schema for PKRT and FKRT\n\t```json\n\t\n\t# this should be written in the target table(GL)\n\t\"foreign_keys_referencing_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"COA\",\n      \"from_column\": \"c3 or any other column in GL which is matched via LLM\"\n      \"linking_column\": \"c3\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"<one description for on relationship like how it is related.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"<many-to-one>\"\n    }\n    ]\n\t```\n\t```json\n\t\"primary_keys_referencing_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"GL\",\n      \"from_column\": \"c3\"\n      \"linking_column\": \"c3 or any other column of LLM result\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"The General Ledger references accounts defined in the Chart of Accounts for financial transactions.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    }\n    ]\n\t```\n\t\n\n```","x":-720,"y":-440,"width":1736,"height":985}
	],
